  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Hebrews",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 3,
    "summary": "Christ is the Apostle and High Priest of our profession—Jesus, being the Son, is more than a servant—Now is the time and the day of our salvation.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Wherefore, holy brethren, partakers of the heavenly calling, consider the Apostle and High Priest of our profession, Christ Jesus;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 61,
            "end": 69,
            "text": "TG Meditation."
          },
          {
            "start": 74,
            "end": 81,
            "text": "TG Jesus Christ, Messenger of the Covenant."
          },
          {
            "start": 86,
            "end": 97,
            "text": "TG High Priest, Melchizedek Priesthood."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Who was faithful to him that appointed him, as also Moses was faithful in all his house.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 70
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For this man was counted worthy of more glory than Moses, inasmuch as he who hath builded the house hath more honour than the house.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 12
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For every house is builded by some man; but he that built all things is God.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 39
          },
          {
            "start": 69,
            "end": 71
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And Moses verily was faithful in all his house, as a servant, for a testimony of those things which were to be spoken after;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 60,
            "text": "TG Servant."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 20
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But Christ as a son over his own house; whose house are we, if we hold fast the confidence and the rejoicing of the hope firm unto the end.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 38,
            "text": "TG Church."
          },
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 51,
            "text": "1 Pet. 2:5 (4–8)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Wherefore (as the Holy Ghost saith, To day if ye will hear his voice,",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 28,
            "text": "Heb. 10:15."
          },
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 42,
            "text": "Ps. 95:7 (7–11)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Harden not your hearts, as in the provocation, in the day of temptation in the wilderness:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 6,
            "text": "TG Hardheartedness."
          },
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 45,
            "text": "Num. 14:23 (2–23); Jacob 1:7 (7–8); Alma 12:36."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "When your fathers tempted me, proved me, and saw my works forty years.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 36,
            "text": "TG Test."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Wherefore I was grieved with that generation, and said, They do alway err in their heart; and they have not known my ways.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 44,
            "text": "Prov. 30:12 (11–14)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 77,
            "end": 82
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "So I sware in my wrath, They shall not enter into my rest.)",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 44,
            "text": "Ps. 95:11."
          },
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 57,
            "text": "D&C 84:24. TG God, Presence of; God, Privilege of Seeing; Rest."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Take heed, brethren, lest there be in any of you an evil heart of unbelief, in departing from the living God.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 62,
            "text": "Gen. 6:5; Matt. 15:19; Hel. 12:4."
          },
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 74,
            "text": "TG Stiffnecked."
          },
          {
            "start": 79,
            "end": 93,
            "text": "GR apostatizing, withdrawing from. TG Apostasy of Individuals."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But exhort one another daily, while it is called To day; lest any of you be hardened through the deceitfulness of sin.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 10,
            "text": "Alma 34:39; D&C 38:23. TG Chastening."
          },
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 55,
            "text": "D&C 45:6."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For we are made partakers of Christ, if we hold the beginning of our confidence steadfast unto the end;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 89,
            "text": "TG Perseverance; Steadfastness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "While it is said, To day if ye will hear his voice, harden not your hearts, as in the provocation.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 52,
            "end": 58,
            "text": "TG Contrite Heart."
          },
          {
            "start": 86,
            "end": 97,
            "text": "TG Provoking."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For some, when they had heard, did provoke: howbeit not all that came out of Egypt by Moses.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But with whom was he grieved forty years? was it not with them that had sinned, whose carcases fell in the wilderness?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 86,
            "end": 94,
            "text": "Num. 14:29 (29, 37); 1 Cor. 10:5 (2–7)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 48
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And to whom sware he that they should not enter into his rest, but to them that believed not?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "So we see that they could not enter in because of unbelief.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 58,
            "text": "TG Unbelief."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
  "nextChapterId": "hebrews4",
  "prevChapterId": "hebrews2",
  "volume": {
    "_id": "newtestament",
    "title": "New Testament",
